{"severity":"error","file":"errors/linear_used_twice_13.march","start_line":15,"start_col":6,"end_line":15,"end_col":35,"message":"The linear value `state.st` is used more than once here.\nLinear values must be consumed exactly once — they cannot be copied or ignored.","code":"linear_used_twice","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/linear_used_twice_13.march","start_line":14,"start_col":19,"end_line":14,"end_col":27,"message":"`state.st` was already consumed here"}],"notes":["`{ state with … }` keeps every field it doesn't replace, so the old `state.st` would survive into the new record. Replace it too: `{ state with st: … }`."]}
